From: Andrea Pesaresi <andreapesaresi82@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ksmbd: return STATUS_INVALID_DEVICE_REQUEST for SMB 2.x
 validate negotiate

Samba clients validate the negotiate exchange after every tree connect on
SMB 2.0.2 and 2.1 sessions as well, not only on SMB 3.0 and 3.0.2.
Releases 4.2.0 to 4.5.10 and 4.6.0 to 4.6.6 accept only
STATUS_FILE_CLOSED, STATUS_INVALID_DEVICE_REQUEST and
STATUS_FS_DRIVER_REQUIRED as a signed "not supported" reply. ksmbd
answers STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED, so those clients fail the tree connect.

Samba fixed the client in 4.5.11, 4.6.7 and 4.7.0 (Samba bug 12808).
The affected releases default to SMB1, so this only matters when the
client is forced to SMB 2.x, e.g. "client max protocol = SMB2".

Return STATUS_INVALID_DEVICE_REQUEST, which every Samba 4 client
accepts. SMB 3.x sessions are not affected.

Signed-off-by: Andrea Pesaresi <andreapesaresi82@gmail.com>
---
 fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
+++ b/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
@@ -8457,8 +8457,14 @@ int smb2_ioctl(struct ksmbd_work *work)
 		break;
 	case FSCTL_VALIDATE_NEGOTIATE_INFO:
 		if (conn->dialect < SMB30_PROT_ID) {
+			/*
+			 * Samba clients 4.2.0 to 4.5.10 and 4.6.0 to 4.6.6
+			 * also validate SMB 2.x sessions and drop the
+			 * connection on STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED.
+			 */
 			ret = -EOPNOTSUPP;
-			goto out;
+			rsp->hdr.Status = STATUS_INVALID_DEVICE_REQUEST;
+			goto out2;
 		}

 		if (in_buf_len < offsetof(struct validate_negotiate_info_req,
